 ### [Sparse Point Set Haptic Rendering via Distance Field](17003-sparse-point-set-haptic-rendering-via-distance-field.md)
-This method provides haptic rendering for sparse, oriented point cloud data by constructing a 3D signed distance field (SDF) on a regular grid using embedded "packing spheres". It solves the problem of generating stable collision forces from incomplete geometric data where traditional mesh-based or dense implicit function methods fail due to sparsity. Unlike sibling methods that rely on dense sampling or explicit surface reconstruction, this technique uses the local normal direction to define minimum-volume spheres that approximate the object's interior, allowing a proxy to be constrained to the zero-iso-surface via gradient descent. See [Sparse Point Set Haptic Rendering via Distance Field](17003-sparse-point-set-haptic-rendering-via-distance-field.md).
